Well, last night I was hooning around in the Gnome town with a couple of wands
of create monster and a co-alligned altar. I had generated oodles of Orcs, and
was busy cleaning up all the equipment. How many times have we all:

1. Pick up all the equipment in a pile.
2. Moved into the shop.
3. Had to then go through our _whole_ equipment list answering yes/no/no/yes...
	etc to then sell all the stuff.

There must be a better way than this!
At the moment, our equipment list is "viewed" by object type, i.e. all the
amulets, then weapons, then armour etc. Wouldn't it be nice is we could view it
in other ways as well. To solve the above problem, view by "most recently
picked up" would be cool. I'm sure there could be advantages in "view by
charges", "view by blessed/uncursed/cursed status", "view by value" etc. I just
can't think of any at the moment...

As an alternative to the problem of selling stuff recently picked up, a change
to the way sacks/chests etc work could solve this. When you apply a sack, and
wish to put something in, the game the askes you what to put in only
_from_your_equipment_list, even if there is stuff in the ground. If the game
first prompted you to pick up the stuff on the ground (like quaffing potions,
for example: "There is a grey potion here. Quaff it?") then we could simply
move over all the stuff we wanted to get into the shop, bung it all in a sack,
and dump the sack in the shop (I presume this sells all the stuff in the sack?)
